WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.760
This variation of English rib produces

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:08.740
a wide, thick, textured fabric that
doesn't have a lot of stretch.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.120
It has the racked texture on one side

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:15.140
and what appears to be one
by one ribbing on the other.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:17.380
It's based on English rib.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.600
Now, English rib is basically ribbing

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:24.620
in a one by one needle arrangement,
tucking every other row on one bed.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:29.060
The tucking can be set up either
on the main bed or the ribber.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:35.220
If you haven't worked English rib,
please watch this video at knititnow.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.620
Com/englishrib.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:41.440
It has tips and tricks for success
with this stitch pattern.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.040
Once you're comfortable with English rib,

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:49.320
try adding some racking to produce
swung English rib.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:55.880
It can be worked by tucking right or left
on either the main bed or the ribber.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.640
No matter which variation you choose

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:01.760
to form this stitch pattern,
you'll be swinging the ribber

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:05.960
with the racking handle
and distorting the stitches.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.980
Start by casting on for one-by-one ribbing
with the method of your choice

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:18.240
end with the carriage on your right and
the ribber set to P5 and knit a few rows.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.000
Be sure you have the outside
needles on the main bed in work.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.080
The needle arrangement
should start like this.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.570
Now, before starting to knit,
let's take a look at our end needles.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:36.480
We'll be racking to seven,
so looking closely, I can see that I need

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:41.200
to pull another needle into work
on the ribber to fill this gap.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.320
Starting with the one-by-one needle set

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:49.850
up, racked to five, I'll set my main
bed to tuck in one direction.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:54.140
For this brother machine,
I'm pushing in the right tuck button.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.200
On a silver machine,

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:59.720
you'll set your cam to tuck
and your right side lever to tuck.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:04.200
I'll knit to the left and both beds knit.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:14.160
Knit to the right and the main bed
has loops over each of the needles.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.300
But wait.
To keep our edges neat and to prevent dropped

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:21.890
stitches, we don't want
to tuck those end needles.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.760
So every time the carriage will be
tucking, in this example,

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:30.500
when the carriage passes right,
I'll pull the end needles all the way out,

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:34.000
and they'll knit while
the rest of the needles tuck.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:44.080
So the first sequence is rack to five,
knit left, all needles will knit,

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.540
pull the end needles out on that main bed,
knit right,

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:55.560
and all of the needles on the main bed
will tuck, except for those end needles.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:04.100
The second sequence is rack
to seven and then knit left.

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:06.440
All needles will knit.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:16.440
Pull the end needles out, knit right,
and all but the end needles will tuck.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:21.200
Repeat sequence one and two
for the stitch pattern.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:24.640
So knit a few inches and then stop.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:30.610
Notice that my edges are neat and tidy
with no dropped stitches and these edges will

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:35.760
easily be seamed or they'll
stand neatly on their own.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.420
You want to experiment a little bit?

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:45.500
Try tucking in the opposite direction
and continue knit for a few inches.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:51.580
Sequence one, we'll tuck left
and knit right, and then rack.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:57.640
Sequence two, again,
we'll tuck left and knit right.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:02.580
When you drop the work from the machine,
by tucking on the main bed,

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:10.560
you'll see that the stitch pattern is
showing on the side away from you.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.280
If you'd prefer to have the stitch pattern

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:19.420
showing on the side towards you,
set your ribber to tuck.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:25.220
Do sequence one and sequence
two tucking on the ribber.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:28.140
Be sure to pull those end needles out

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.720
and align that end those
end needles as you need to.

